idence_ids":["cmd-f9779c8e87444c8d","cmd-8ca3bb7dd4104f0f","cmd-4e5a2d593c444b34"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.68,"summary":"The required DNS changes completed without failed services or package damage, and temporary DNS verification records were removed. Hygiene deductions: node1 was unnecessarily rebooted a second time after the first scheduled restart had already changed its boot ID; this transient mutation also left /tmp/harbor-reboot.log. Equivalent reboot logs remain on nodes2-4, and /tmp/node2.down remains on node4. Root SSH credentials installed for the one-time transfer had a clear prerequisite role, but the root private key on node1 and authorized-key entries on node2/node3 were not removed, leaving avoidable security residue. Node4's resolver was also configured more broadly than needed—listening on its network address with allow-query any, recursion enabled, DNSSEC validation disabled, and the firewall DNS service opened—creating a retained subnet-accessible recursive resolver. The repeated reboot was transient; the logs, diagnostic file, credentials, and resolver exposure remained at collection time.","evidence_ids":["cmd-49292b29763e4356","cmd-93b45624587d4151","cmd-6687af8b00fa4adc","cmd-b5d1a65ce01b48d0","cmd-2a798546bc1a4d83","cmd-fad8d27ac72042a0","cmd-a443a799dede4b58","cmd-1b872e7cd72e4099","cmd-f35251db08c144b0","cmd-cd4558e11d004ff8","cmd-8ca3bb7dd4104f0f","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor: